If I return a promise in an exercise, it just prints out the fact that the object is a promise. I'd suggest that we could wait on the promise evaluation and then return the result or error.

e.g. I have to do this if I want to see the value of a promise:

```
library(promises)

done <- FALSE

myPromiseHere() %>% then(function(v){
  print("DONE")
  print(v)
}, function(e){
  print("ERROR")
  print(e)
}) %>% finally(function(){
  done <<- TRUE  
})

while (!done){
  later::run_now()
}
```

